{"label":"1C","direction":"supports","claim":"Tempus calls its new rare-disease whole-genome test small, so WGS adds little sequencing volume in 2026.","detail":"CEO Lefkofsky said GenomeNext volume ran about 50% above the internal first-month expectation 2–3 weeks in. He also said 'when you get to market and sell 500 or 1,000 tests, that's a good start' and called these 'small numbers.' At about 100–125 Gb per 30x genome (known), 1,000 genomes is ~0.10–0.125M Gb, or about 0.01–0.02% of the ~800M Gb high-throughput base cited in the exclusion list. That arithmetic is mine. Tempus has one month of data and is 'being conservative' on whole-genome estimates, so WGS cannot offset slowing volume at a top-3 oncology lab in 2026.","url":"https://allmind.ai/earnings/event/2940116","date":"2026-07-30","source_name":"Allmind transcript, Tempus Q2'26 call","source_type":"earnings_call","quote":"when you get to market and sell 500 or 1,000 tests, that's a good start","strength":"medium","why_new":"The known file says only that Tempus WGS has one month of data. This adds the 500–1,000 test scale and a Gb sizing."},
{"label":"1C","direction":"supports","claim":"Tempus says whole genome is not cannibalizing exome, so it adds little net Gb, and management is waiting to see.","detail":"Lefkofsky said 'right now, it's not cannibalistic to our whole exome business' and described a 'wait and see' stance. The upside he sees from whole genomes is an H2'26 item and is not in guidance. Exome-to-genome migration is the main way WGS could lift clinical Gb, and it has not begun at this lab.","url":"https://allmind.ai/earnings/event/2940116","date":"2026-07-30","source_name":"Allmind transcript, Tempus Q2'26 call","source_type":"earnings_call","quote":"Right now, it's not cannibalistic to our whole exome business","strength":"weak","why_new":"No known item covers Tempus's exome-vs-genome cannibalization comment."},
{"label":"1C","direction":"supports","claim":"Only about 10% of Tempus's sales force sells MRD, and MRD volume is still ~9K tests a quarter.","detail":"MRD ran ~6,500 tests in Q1 and ~9,000 in Q2'26 (+38% q/q). Management says 'only about 10% of our sales force is selling MRD today' on reimbursed indications. Against Natera's 283K MRD tests in Q2'26 (known), Tempus MRD is ~3% of Natera's volume. That supports the thesis point that MRD is not yet a meaningful share of lab mix beyond Natera. Management says MRD is a '$20 billion plus market' and wants scaling timed to break-even ASPs, so ramp spending is deliberately paced.","url":"https://allmind.ai/earnings/event/2940116","date":"2026-07-30","source_name":"Allmind transcript, Tempus Q2'26 call","source_type":"earnings_call","quote":"only about 10% of our sales force is selling MRD today","strength":"medium","why_new":"The 9K figure is known. The 10% sales-force coverage, 38% q/q growth and break-even-ASP pacing are new."},
{"label":"1C","direction":"against","claim":"Tempus oncology volume growth accelerated to 31% from 28% in Q1, so a large Illumina customer is speeding up.","detail":"The Q2'26 press release gives oncology volume +31% y/y vs +28% in Q1'26 and MRD 9,000 vs 6,500. Total revenue was $382.5M (+22%) and FY26 guidance was raised to $1.595–1.605B. This does not show a volume slowdown at this customer. It matches Natera and Guardant strength, so any Illumina volume slowdown has to come from mix, price and region.","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001717115/000119312526326083/tem-ex99_1.htm","date":"2026-07-30","source_name":"Tempus 8-K Ex. 99.1","source_type":"filing","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"The known file has Tempus oncology +31% but not the sequential acceleration from +28%."},
{"label":"1B","direction":"supports","claim":"Tempus Diagnostics gross margin rose about 3.8 points y/y, which suggests falling unit cost at a big oncology lab.","detail":"Diagnostics GAAP gross margin was 62.6% vs 58.8% in Q2'25 (non-GAAP 63.9% vs 59.4%). Diagnostics cost of revenue rose only 8.5% ($108.2M vs $99.8M) while oncology volume grew 31%. Cost per unit therefore fell on rough math: 1.085/1.31 = 0.83, about −17%, though the mix includes hereditary and other tests. Sequencing cost is not broken out. Lower unit cost at a large customer supports the thesis that price and productivity gains are being kept by labs, which feeds their pricing leverage over Illumina.","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001717115/000119312526326083/tem-ex99_1.htm","date":"2026-07-30","source_name":"Tempus 8-K Ex. 99.1","source_type":"filing","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"The known file has Tempus oncology volume and a job posting but no unit-cost or margin series."},
